build/
# SAN-1: separate sanitizer build trees (make ubsan / make asan), so their
# objects never land in build/ and a subsequent plain `make` stays correct.
build-ubsan/
build-asan/
# [TT-7]: build-san/ is the combined ASan+UBSan tree (make san), same shape.
build-san/
*.o
*.a
# Core dumps only — anchored, because an unanchored `core` also matches the
# DIRECTORY src/core/, which silently kept the whole pipeline driver
# (arena.c, compile.c, sb.c, internal.h) out of every commit. A fresh clone
# of this repo did not build until M2.8 caught it.
/core
/core.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
tests/fuzz/failures/

# The session hand-off brief: deliberately NOT project record, so it must not
# be committed. It was, twice, on 2026-08-10 — `git add -A -- docs` stages it,
# and the previous session's brief warned about exactly that in prose. A rule
# a tool enforces beats a rule a comment states.
/docs/dev/wake.md
worktrees/
scripts/tests/*.testreport
build-ccache/

# [DD-14 wave F] the email specimen's SUBJECT FILES are derived, not source:
# 372 KB of binaries `gen_subjects.py` reproduces deterministically, whose
# integrity check is the COMMITTED manifest.tsv. tests/recursion/gen_corpus.py
# regenerates them on demand when it needs them for realworld.rxt.
docs/design/subroutines_measurements/email_specimen/subjects/
# [DD-14 wave G] and its THROUGHPUT subjects for the same reason, one order of
# magnitude larger: 3 MB of deterministic filler that
# `gen_throughput_subjects.py` reproduces and that
# `tests/recursion/run_specimen_identity.sh` regenerates when it times them.
docs/design/subroutines_measurements/email_specimen/throughput/

# lane hold/lift artifacts (manager<->lane signalling files, never content)
# 2026-08-31: .hold and rulings.md added after both were swept into a lane's
# commit (the block predated those two spellings; opt5s1's root-cause).
.lift
.hold_ack
.hold
# 2026-09-03: .stage joined on the same argument — it is the manager's
# watchdog/next-lane liveness channel (a lane writes its current stage name
# into it at every boundary), so it is signalling and never content.
.stage
/rulings.md

# the manager -> lane rulings channel: polled, never committed (its own header says so)
docs/dev/lanes/opt5i_rulings.md
docs/dev/lanes/isl1_rulings.md
